  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "We cannot drop `channel` from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Why this change is blocked\n\n1. **Downstream Cross-Repository Consumers**: Even though `channel` is not read elsewhere within `orders-service`, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is published to Kafka (`orders.placed`) and actively consumed by `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. Dropping the field is a breaking change for deployed consumers.\n2. **Order Model Dependency**: The [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) event factory relies on `order.channel` from the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model, which in turn comes from [`NewOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/order.ts#L32-L38) on `POST /orders`. Removing `channel` from the model would break the published event.\n\n### Compliant Path Forward\n\nTo retire `channel` in accordance with ARCH-4:\n\n1. **Deprecation Phase**: Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/events.ts#L16) and notify the teams owning `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`.\n2. **Consumer Migration**: Allow the downstream services to deploy updates that remove their dependency on `channel`.\n3. **Removal**: Once all consumers have migrated and the deprecation period has concluded, remove `channel` from the event schema and the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w4/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model.\n",
